1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,370
Hold.

2
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:07,400
What?

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,970
Explain your sneeze.

4
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:10,710
I'm sorry?

5
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,410
- Do you have allergies?  - No.

6
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:13,940
Is there too much pepper on your salad?

7
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:15,080
I don't put pepper on salads.

8
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,280
I've heard enough. Sit over there.

9
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,980
Oh, come on.I don't want to sit by myself.

10
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:21,080
That's what Typhoid Mary said,

11
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,990
And clearly, her friends buckled.

12
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,650
Guys, help me.

13
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:25,820
Sheldon, come on.

14
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,290
Yeah, it's just one sneeze.

15
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,290
- You're on your own. - See you, buddy.

16
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:33,030
Oh, Leonard, I have something for you.

17
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:37,600
Per our roommate agreement, this is your 24-hour notice that I will be having

18
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,940
A non-related female spending two nights in our apartment.

19
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:45,140
When you say "non-related female,"

20
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,880
You still mean human, right?

21
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,140
Of course.

22
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:51,150
Pets are banned under the roommate agreement,

23
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:54,250
With the exception of service animals, such as seeing eye dogs

24
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,420
And, one day, cybernetically-enhanced helper monkeys.

25
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:01,690
Are you planning on kidnapping a woman?

26
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:02,990
Sarcasm?

27
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:06,660
Yes, but mixed with genuine concern.

28
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:11,800
For your information, I'll be playing host to Dr. Elizabeth Plimpton.

29
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,040
The cosmological physicist from Princeton?

30
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,040
Yes.

31
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,310
And until you acquire a surgical mask,

32
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:19,640
Please address your comments to me through a napkin.

33
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:23,980
We've been corresponding for years about our mutual interest in

34
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:27,450
Gravitational wave signatures of inflatons in the early universe.

35
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:31,090
And now she's under consideration for a position at our university.

36
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,790
Why didn't you tell me you knew Elizabeth Plimpton?

37
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:36,030
I am a huge fan of hers!

38
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:38,360
I didn't realize I was obligated to share my connection

39
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,460
With things you're a fan of, but very well.

40
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:42,060
You enjoy Canadian bacon.

41
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,830
I've been to Toronto.

42
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:46,340
Okay, fine. Where is she going to sleep?

43
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,850
My room, of course.

44
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:49,640
Holy crap!

45
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:54,710
Holy crap!

46
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:57,080
Yeah, um, I have a two-part question.

47
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,080
Go ahead.

48
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,580
A: Are you kidding me?

49
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:02,990
And B: Seriously, are you freaking kidding me?

50
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:05,770
A: I rarely kid.

51
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:10,030
And B: When I do kid, you will know it by my use of the word "bazinga."

52
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:14,460
So you're saying the two of you are going to be sleeping in the same bed?

53
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,130
Yes.

54
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:17,300
Bazinga.

55
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:22,670
Leonard?

56
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:25,410
Thank you.

57
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:27,340
Why is a world-renowned scientist

58
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:29,350
Staying in our apartment instead of a hotel?

59
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:30,980
Well, she doesn't care for hotels.

60
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,250
And who can blame her?

61
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,320
Windows that don't open,

62
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,850
Multi-user linens,

63
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:37,550
Keys shaped like credit cards-- as if one walks around

64
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:39,760
With unassigned slots in one's wallet.

65
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,120
All right, I believe I have time

66
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,160
For one more question.

67
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,890
Yes, Raj?

68
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:47,830
When can I sit with you again?

69
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:50,500
When I've seen Two consecutive negative throat cultures

70
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,400
Spaced 12 hours apart. You know the drill.

71
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:56,140
All right, if you'll excuse me, I am off to start

72
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:58,910
A prophylactic course of antibiotics.

73
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:03,780
I can't believe he's friends with elizabeth plimpton.

74
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:06,480
I can't believe they let him into canada.

75
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,050
Whoa, whoa, whoa. You heard the man.

76
00:03:08,050 --> 00:03:09,590
Where's your throat cultures?

77
00:03:10,550 --> 00:03:12,590
Kidding. Sit down.

78
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,100
Hey, Sheldon.

79
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,870
Oh, Penny, excellent.

80
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:53,140
I have a question about these maxi pads.

81
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,740
Are the wings truly functional

82
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:58,410
Or have I fallen victim to marketing hype?

83
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,550
What?

84
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:02,180
Why are you doing with-- what?

85
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,890
The stock boy at Walgreens

86
00:04:03,890 --> 00:04:05,990
Was frustratingly uninformed on the subject.

87
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:08,860
Sheldon, what are you doing with maxi pads?

88
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:13,610
I have a lady friend who will be staying with me for a few days.

89
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,330
What?

90
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:17,100
I want her to feel at home.

91
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:21,170
I also bought scented soaps, pantyhose, midol,

92
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:24,540
Calcium chews and what is apparently a yogurt

93
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:27,780
Specifically designed to regulate the female bowel.

94
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,210
Wait, wait, hold on, back up.

95
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:33,180
You're having a woman stay with you?

96
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:34,220
Yes.

97
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:36,220
Why does that seem to flabbergast everybody?

98
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:37,950
Oh... no, no, no, no.

99
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:39,190
I'm not flabbergasted.

100
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:40,790
I'm... puzzled.

101
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:43,760
Yeah, let's go with puzzled.

102
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:44,830
A word of warning.

103
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:46,760
My guest is a noted physicist

104
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,900
And the leading expert on quantum cosmology,

105
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,900
So please try to avoid wasting her time

106
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:54,270
With female jibber jabber.

107
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:55,900
Female jibber jabber?

108
00:04:55,910 --> 00:04:57,240
Shoe sales, hair styles,

109
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:01,380
Mud masks, gossip about your friends Brad and Angelina.

110
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:04,950
Oh, they're not my friends.

111
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:08,420
I'm not surprised, considering the way you talk about them behind their backs.

112
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,570
She's here, she's here.

113
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:15,740
How do I look? Do I look smart?

114
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:20,010
Oh, good grief. This isn't about you.

115
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:21,040
Coming!

116
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,110
Now, listen.

117
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:23,460
One of the great minds of the 21st century

118
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:28,850
is about to play host to one of the other great minds of the 21st century.

119
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:30,690
So pay attention.

120
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:35,290
Years from now, my biographer might ask you about this event.

121
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:39,130
Oh, I have so many things to tell your biographer.

122
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:43,570
Dr. Cooper, thank goodness. I completely forgot your address.

123
00:05:43,570 --> 00:05:46,200
But then I remembered that I'd written it on my hand.

124
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,470
Lucky for me,

125
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:49,490
I didn't confuse it with what I'd written on my other hand,

126
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:52,710
which are the coordinates for a newly discovered neutron star.

127
00:05:52,710 --> 00:05:55,610
'cause if I tried to go there, I'd be crushed by hypergravity.

128
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,950
- Anyway, hello. - Hello.

129
00:05:58,950 --> 00:06:00,850
Nice to finally meet you in person.

130
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:02,380
I would imagine it is.

131
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:07,720
This is my friend and roommate, Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

132
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,660
Hi-lo.

133
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:12,290
I-I started to say "hi,"

134
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,600
and then I switched to "hello" in the middle.

135
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,570
It came out "hi-lo."

136
00:06:18,970 --> 00:06:21,540
Uh, it's nice to meet you.

137
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:23,970
I-I've read both your books and most of your papers.

138
00:06:23,970 --> 00:06:27,780
I-I'm Leonard, I live here, you're brilliant.

139
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:28,840
I apologize.

140
00:06:28,850 --> 00:06:31,310
He's only an experimental physicist.

141
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:32,850
No need to apologize.

142
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,550
Some of my best friends are experimental physicists.

143
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:38,550
Well, not my best friends, but I know them.

144
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,490
My best friend is

145
00:06:40,490 --> 00:06:42,190
a molecular chemist named Wendy.

146
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:44,190
I'm sorry, I'm rambling.

147
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,190
Hi-lo.

148
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:47,800
Are you hungry, thirsty?

149
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:49,000
Can I offer you anything?

150
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,170
No, she's my guest.

151
00:06:50,170 --> 00:06:51,970
If anyone should offer her anything, it should be me.

152
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:53,900
Elizabeth, can I get you something?

153
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,440
Perhaps a feminine hygiene product

154
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:58,110
or a bowel-regulating yogurt?

155
00:06:58,110 --> 00:06:59,880
Interesting choices.

156
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:02,740
Based on my current needs, I guess I'd pick the yogurt.

157
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:03,750
Excellent.

158
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:05,080
If the yogurt works,

159
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:07,880
I bought some delightful scented candles.

160
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:14,690
Look, it's you.

161
00:07:17,230 --> 00:07:20,160
Thank you so much for opening up your home to me.

162
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:23,230
Well, who wants to stay in a hotel?

163
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:26,970
Windows that don't open, those crazy card-shaped keys.

164
00:07:26,970 --> 00:07:28,400
I'm so glad you understand.

165
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,810
No, he doesn't understand.

166
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:31,840
I understand.

167
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,040
Well, I understand, too.

168
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,640
You're just misappropriating my understanding.

169
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:40,420
I think any university would want you.

170
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:43,250
Except, of course, any university that had already had you.

171
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:47,190
Because they would've already wanted you before they, you know, got you.

172
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:51,630
From the mind that brought you "hi-lo."

173
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:55,200
Let me show you to your room.

174
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,300
All right.

175
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,200
I guess I am tired. Good night, Leonard.

176
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,970
Uh, sleep night.

177
00:07:59,970 --> 00:08:01,570
I mean, obviously, good night.

178
00:08:01,570 --> 00:08:02,870
I started to say "sleep tight,"

179
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:04,840
then I changed my mind in the middle.

180
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,080
I swear to god, I'm smart.

181
00:08:09,910 --> 00:08:11,550
Get it together, man.

182
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:16,790
All right, let me show you

183
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:18,990
some of the features of the room.

184
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:20,560
First, windows.

185
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,560
Conventional.

186
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,190
Open, closed.

187
00:08:23,190 --> 00:08:24,490
Open, closed.

188
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:25,930
Halfway open.

189
00:08:25,930 --> 00:08:28,660
Or halfway closed, depending on your philosophical bent.

190
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,970
Over here is my comic book collection. Feel free to browse.

191
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,070
There's a box of disposable reading gloves

192
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:37,540
on the night stand.

193
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:39,040
Good to know.

194
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:42,480
In here, you'll find emergency provisions.

195
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,510
An eight-day supply of food and water, a crossbow,

196
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:50,120
Season 2 of Star Trek the original series on a high-density flash drive.

197
00:08:50,850 --> 00:08:53,990
What if there's a disaster that destroys all the USB ports?

198
00:08:53,990 --> 00:08:56,890
Then there's really no reason to live, is there?

199
00:08:56,890 --> 00:08:59,730
Can I ask a question about your roommate?

200
00:08:59,730 --> 00:09:02,460
He's an odd duck, isn't he?

201
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:04,630
What's his relationship status?

202
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:07,570
Well, there was a misbegotten adventure

203
00:09:07,570 --> 00:09:09,800
With a waitress who lives across the hall.

204
00:09:09,810 --> 00:09:12,070
It ended as inexplicably as it began.

205
00:09:12,070 --> 00:09:13,810
They had very little in common,

206
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:15,610
except for carnal activity.

207
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:16,680
That's why I acquired

208
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:19,150
these noise-canceling headphones.

209
00:09:19,150 --> 00:09:20,980
If you decide to use them,

210
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,750
please clean the ear pieces afterwards

211
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,890
with the wet wipes you'll find in the bathroom.

212
00:09:24,890 --> 00:09:27,360
They're in the drawer labeled "wet wipes."

213
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,720
Okay.

214
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:31,630
Good. I'll leave you to your nighttime ablutions.

215
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:33,860
I've e-mailed you the morning bathroom schedule.

216
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:37,600
You'll also find a laminated copy in your welcome packet.

217
00:09:39,170 --> 00:09:41,940
It's on the back of the emergency escape route diagram.

218
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:42,970
How thoughtful.

219
00:09:42,970 --> 00:09:45,170
- Sleep well, my friend.  - You, too.

220
00:09:46,010 --> 00:09:49,410
Oh, let me just get one thing.

221
00:09:49,410 --> 00:09:51,910
It's my backup emergency supply kit.

222
00:09:51,910 --> 00:09:55,220
The living room escape route doesn't pass through here.

223
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,450
Now, good night.

224
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:58,920
And if there's an apocalypse, good luck.

225
00:10:04,530 --> 00:10:05,990
Yes?

226
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,900
I saw your light on.

227
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,170
Is everything all right?

228
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:12,030
Yeah, I just couldn't sleep.

229
00:10:12,030 --> 00:10:13,870
Me neither.

230
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:15,570
Oh, look what I'm reading.

231
00:10:15,570 --> 00:10:17,310
It's you.

232
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:18,940
I thought you already read it.

233
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:20,340
I did, but it's been a while,

234
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:23,910
And I wanted to sound smart over breakfast.

235
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,910
Aw, you're smart.

236
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,980
Oh, good.

237
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,580
Wasn't sure it was coming across.

238
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:30,890
What chapter are you on?

239
00:10:30,890 --> 00:10:32,420
Uh, six.

240
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:36,420
Oh, the extragalactic distance ladder.

241
00:10:36,430 --> 00:10:38,030
Want to know a little secret?

242
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:39,760
Sure.

243
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:43,330
I wrote the section on the Wilson-Bappu effect completely naked.

244
00:10:46,170 --> 00:10:48,270
Really?

245
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:50,510
Uh, sure doesn't read that way.

246
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:52,470
Here, let me show you.

247
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:57,050
When we consider the brightness of pulsating variable stars,

248
00:10:57,050 --> 00:10:59,250
we start to see a possible explanation

249
00:10:59,250 --> 00:11:03,990
for some of the discrepancies found in Hubble's constant.

250
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:10,330
You really make science come alive.

251
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:36,200
Vocal test. Morning vocal test.

252
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:37,640
Second vocal test.

253
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,370
Second morning vocal test.

254
00:11:39,370 --> 00:11:40,870
Morning, Sheldon.

255
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:41,910
Morning.

256
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:42,940
Morning, Sheldon.

257
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,880
Morning.

258
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:45,380
I trust you had a pleasant night.

259
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,510
More than pleasant.

260
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:55,120
Excuse me, I'm going to relieve myself.

261
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:57,790
How do you take your coffee?

262
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,830
- Black. - Okeydoke.

263
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:04,360
Pee for Houston, pee for Austin,

264
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:07,500
pee for the state my heart got lost in.

265
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:13,140
And shake twice for Texas.

266
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:20,610
Something his mother taught him.

267
00:12:21,710 --> 00:12:24,850
All right, Elizabeth, the bathroom is yours.

268
00:12:24,850 --> 00:12:28,150
The seat is down, and has been sanitized for your protection.

269
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:31,120
That's very thoughtful, but I think I'll finish my coffee first.

270
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:35,260
Ah, so the yogurt didn't work.

271
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:39,630
